{"id": "EUVD-2026-106083", "enisaUuid": "b136f448-e2f2-3ecd-93ba-12803a14aa12", "description": "Vulnerability in the MySQL Server, MySQL Cluster product of Oracle MySQL (component: Client programs).  Supported versions that are affected are MySQL Server: 8.4.0-8.4.12, 9.7.0-9.7.3, 26.7.0-26.7.1; MySQL Cluster: 8.0.0-8.0.49, 8.4.0-8.4.12, 9.7.0-9.7.3 and  26.7.0-26.7.1. Easily exploitable vulnerability allows unauthenticated attacker with network access via multiple protocols to compromise MySQL Server, MySQL Cluster.  Successful attacks of this vulnerability can result in unauthorized ability to cause a hang or frequently repeatable crash (complete DOS) of MySQL Server, MySQL Cluster. CVSS 3.1 Base Score 7.5 (Availability impacts).  CVSS Vector: (CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H).", "datePublished": "2026-10-20T21:22:16", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T18:50:22", "baseScore": 7.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://www.oracle.com/security-alerts/cpuoct2026.html"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-101679", "GHSA-pwv9-2jx3-8439"], "assigner": "oracle", "epss": 0.43, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "471eebb6-8462-3779-82ce-244538791c22", "product": {"name": "MySQL Cluster", "vendor": {"name": "Oracle Corporation"}}, "product_version": "9.7.0-9.7.3"}, {"id": "736ba34a-2a58-3095-b983-c7bf02f3c4f5", "product": {"name": "MySQL Server", "vendor": {"name": "Oracle Corporation"}}, "product_version": "8.4.0-8.4.12"}, {"id": "7aeae226-5553-3451-b980-23a46b872110", "product": {"name": "MySQL Server", "vendor": {"name": "Oracle Corporation"}}, "product_version": "9.7.0-9.7.3"}, {"id": "9d89977d-a5f5-349c-a85c-660971176f14", "product": {"name": "MySQL Cluster", "vendor": {"name": "Oracle Corporation"}}, "product_version": "8.0.0-8.0.49"}, {"id": "9ede77f8-3fdc-3dd0-9de7-d52a653fd8f7", "product": {"name": "MySQL Cluster", "vendor": {"name": "Oracle Corporation"}}, "product_version": "8.4.0-8.4.12"}, {"id": "c